xnu 0198: the GPU hardware init kgsl runs and the shim never did

The 71-dword client stream completes in 14 ms. The 168-dword one -- the first
stream that draws, `CP_SET_DRAW_STATE` then `CP_DRAW_INDX_OFFSET` -- never
writes its fence, and every submission after it is refused. The shim loads the
SQE and sets `CP_SQE_CNTL=1`, but never runs the register programming
`gen7_start` does first and never sends `CP_ME_INIT`; a draw is the first thing
that puts UCHE/RB/SP/TPL1/GRAS to work at the chip's bank interleave, and all of
those blocks still hold the bootloader's reset values.

Program what `gen7_start` programs (GBIF QOS, UCHE trap and write-thru base,
UCHE cache ways and CMDQ config, the `NC_MODE_CNTL` set for highest bank bit 14,
the hang-detect counter, `CP_APRIV_CNTL`/`CP_BV_APRIV_CNTL`), then, at
`gpuinit=2`, send `CP_THREAD_CONTROL(BIT(27))` and `CP_ME_INIT` through the ring
without a power-up reglist and prove the ring still runs with one
memwrite-plus-fence submission. `gpuinit=1` is the register programming alone,
because the two halves fail differently on blocks this board has never touched.

The `CP_ME_INIT` packet goes at the ring cursor the 2000-submission stress left
(`mondrian_uc_at`), not at this function's own `at`: writing behind
`CP_RB_RPTR` and then lowering `CP_RB_WPTR` makes the SQE reinterpret the ring
and the next client stream wedges.

